{"answers":[{"answer":"Yes: \"The system shall be sized for 5,000 devices reporting at once.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-13","question":"Does the request ask for this: Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume."},{"answer":"Split the full scope across about four runs; keep all requirements.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-9","question":"The 28 requirements are estimated at about four runs of work. How would you like the scope handled?"},{"answer":"Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-10","question":"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser?"},{"answer":"Flag the gap for review and show the API-returned stock status; do not automatically place the stock On Hold.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-11","question":"When a temperature-history gap affects stock, should the stock be automatically placed On Hold while the gap is unresolved, or should the gap be flagged for review without automatically changing stock status?"},{"answer":"Require effective dates to be today or later; do not recalculate earlier decisions.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-12","question":"May a temperature-profile version have an effective date in the past, and if so, how should recalculated results affect stock that was already released or had a quality decision?"}],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-14","impact":3,"impactReason":"This determines whether restricted quantities are recorded as delivered or remain outstanding.","options":["Do not mark the delivery as completed; show the returned restriction and leave the affected quantity outstanding for follow-up.","Record the reported handover as an exception for quality review, without treating it as an approved delivery.","Allow the handover to count as completed despite the returned restriction, and show the restriction as a warning."],"reason":"This is the smallest behavior consistent with the requirement that affected stock cannot be handed over until quality staff decide its disposition.","recommended":"Do not mark the delivery as completed; show the returned restriction and leave the affected quantity outstanding for follow-up.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"If an offline handover is queued and the API returns a restriction because the stock went On Hold or was recalled, how should the app handle that recorded handover?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-15","impact":3,"impactReason":"This determines how long recipient PII remains on the browser and what additional protection applies to it.","options":["Keep the existing same-driver access rule and retain queued actions until sync or API rejection/refusal; add no local encryption or expiry.","Encrypt queued actions in browser storage and retain them until sync or API rejection/refusal.","Encrypt queued actions in browser storage and delete them after 7 days if they are still unsynced."],"reason":"This preserves the existing retention decision without adding unrequested storage mechanisms or risking loss of offline work.","recommended":"Keep the existing same-driver access rule and retain queued actions until sync or API rejection/refusal; add no local encryption or expiry.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Q-10 settles that queued actions stay tied to the originating driver across sign-out and workday end, and are erased or rejected if access is refused or the account is disabled. Should any additional local protection or expiry rule apply to queued actions containing recipient names on a shared browser?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"Handovers recorded offline are queued and synced later, but AC-16.5 and AC-6.4 rely on a returned 'handover restriction' for stock that went On Hold or was recalled, so an offline driver can hand over held or recalled stock and nothing says what happens to that handover when it syncs.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"The ears says cached route and delivery data are cleared at sign-out, workday end or refused access, yet unsynced queued actions, which hold recipient names (PII), are kept on a possibly shared browser with no limit on how long they stay or how they are protected.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-24 and REQ-3 cite ASM-1/ASM-17 ('No; online only'), and the spec's assumptions still list that text, which contradicts the Q-10 decision to keep an offline queue tied to the driver that REQ-24 is built on.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'The cached workday ends' triggers clearing data and keeping the queue, but nothing defines when a workday ends (warehouse time zone, route completion or a clock time) or what happens to a queue whose driver never signs in again.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-24.2 and the ears refer to 'supported' loading and delivery actions without listing which actions work offline, so no test can check offline coverage.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The assumptions say 'the source request ends during US-009' and cite 'US-001' for sign-in, but no such stories appear in the intent artifact, so the driver and authentication behaviour rest on sources nobody can check.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The one-time-code second step and staff Microsoft sign-in are justified by 'US-001', which is not in the artifacts, and ASM-23's answer (email and password, reset link, no SSO) never mentions a one-time code.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":5,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-2.2 covers only the code challenge and never says what the screen shows for a wrong or expired one-time code, a code resend, a failed Microsoft sign-in or a session timeout.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'the Meridian Microsoft sign-in option' fixes one identity tenant in the requirement, and nothing says the tenant or provider identifiers come from configuration.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-3.2 gives Quality Managers and Auditors all-warehouse visibility, but no intent span, answer or assumption sets that scope rule.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"I-7 asks for role and warehouse access controls, but no requirement gives System Administrators screens to create staff users, assign roles or assign warehouses; only customer user invitations exist (REQ-4).","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-18.2 states a safety margin that 'defaults to 4 hours', a value found in no intent span, answer or assumption.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-18.3 covers route changes only 'before the driver has left for an affected stop' and never says what the screen does when a change is attempted after the driver has left.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Box types and qualified durations, the safety margin, warehouse cut-offs, holidays, time zones, vehicles and drivers are all called 'configured', but no requirement gives anyone a screen to maintain them.","reqId":"REQ-17","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-17.3's 'shows exactly one logger requirement' names no visible element or text that a test could check.","reqId":"REQ-17","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-21 and REQ-22 cite ASM-18 ('keep affected stock On Hold until resolved') as a source even though they implement the opposite decision from Q-11 and ASM-2.","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-22 repeats REQ-21's rule against showing an estimated tier for an unresolved gap almost word for word, leaving two sources for one rule that can drift apart.","reqId":"REQ-22","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"To reconcile ASM-9 (images and PDFs) with ASM-21 (supplier export format), the spec invents a separate 'receipt-evidence' upload that no intent span asks for, and admits the logger format contract 'needs confirmation'.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":4,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-7.2 covers only a receipt accepted with a logger file and never says what happens when a receipt is submitted without an inbound logger file or with one that has no readings.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"A move between cold rooms gives portions different temperature histories, which under Q-5 should split the handling unit, but REQ-12 says nothing about splitting and has no error path for moving held or quarantined stock or more than is on hand.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-13.3 has a Dispatcher opening an order form, but REQ-14 only lets customer users create orders, so a Dispatcher order form is never defined.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-13.1 lets Customer Administrators remove or edit saved addresses without saying what happens to open orders or routes that already use that address.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-14.3's next-working-day and after-cut-off rules come from 'the specified delivery and order rules' (I-10), which appear in no artifact, and the web app is asked to re-apply a rule the API already enforces.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Customers may change or cancel only 'before Packed', and Dispatchers may cancel after Packed, but neither rule is anchored, the cited source Q-6 is about addresses and shelf life, and the order status lifecycle is never defined.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No intent span or answer asks for customers to see internal quality-review cases on delivered orders.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-25 has no validation path for a blank recipient name, an unchecked acknowledgment, or delivered plus undelivered quantities that do not equal the planned quantity.","reqId":"REQ-25","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-25.4 shows the warehouse receipt for returned undelivered stock, but no requirement defines a return-receipt flow, and REQ-7's receipt form covers inbound supplier lots only.","reqId":"REQ-25","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-26.2 combines ASM-15 (accept the stated response and disposition as accounted for) with ASM-19 (require a categorised quantity reconciliation), so it is unclear whether a response without the full reconciliation counts as accounted for.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-26.6 lets a Quality Manager close a recall without saying whether closing is allowed while quantities are still unreconciled, or whether a customer can correct a response already submitted.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The recall response form has no error path for a customer entering a quantity above what was delivered to them.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-9.4 passes on 'shows the returned error message or disables the approval control', so two different behaviours both pass and the criterion cannot pin down what the screen does.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-10.1 and AC-10.2 never say what the screen shows when no rows match a filter or when the returned status quantities do not add up to on-hand.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The ears promises 'silence status', but no acceptance criterion checks it, and AC-19.2's 'without presenting excluded readings as calculation inputs' names no visible element a test could look for.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-27.1's 'the displayed or filtered records' leaves open whether the CSV holds the current page or the whole filtered set, and nothing says which roles may export PII such as recipient names.","reqId":"REQ-27","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-5.6's 'before today' does not say whose time zone defines today (the user's, the warehouse's or UTC) when checking an effective date.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"'1,000 users' does not say concurrent or total, and '5,000 devices reporting at once' gives no web-side measure such as page load time or payload size that a test could check.","reqId":"NFR-4","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"blocking":true,"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 28 requirements, about 4 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","fails":["This spec has 28 requirements, about 4 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."],"passed":false},{"blocking":true,"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","fails":[],"hint":"Each Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes.","passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]}},"problemOf":{"Q-14":[1],"Q-15":[2]},"problems":[{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-24","text":"Handovers recorded offline are queued and synced later, but AC-16.5 and AC-6.4 rely on a returned 'handover restriction' for stock that went On Hold or was recalled, so an offline driver can hand over held or recalled stock and nothing says what happens to that handover when it syncs."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-24","text":"The ears says cached route and delivery data are cleared at sign-out, workday end or refused access, yet unsynced queued actions, which hold recipient names (PII), are kept on a possibly shared browser with no limit on how long they stay or how they are protected."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-2","text":"The one-time-code second step and staff Microsoft sign-in are justified by 'US-001', which is not in the artifacts, and ASM-23's answer (email and password, reset link, no SSO) never mentions a one-time code."}],"round":2,"settled":[{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The system shall be sized for 5,000 devices reporting at once.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.","ref":"Q-13"},{"decision":"The 28 requirements are estimated at about four runs of work. How would you like the scope handled? → Split the full scope across about four runs; keep all requirements.","how":"answered","kind":"lint","problem":"L9 size: This spec has 28 requirements, about 4 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","ref":"Q-9"},{"decision":"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser? → Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"AC-24.8 keeps queued actions, which contain recipient names, after sign-out or a disabled account and later tries to sync them, contradicting REQ-3's rule to clear protected data when access is refused and ASM-17's rule that a disabled driver's queued actions are not accepted.","ref":"Q-10"},{"decision":"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser? → Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"After a driver signs out with actions still queued, nothing says whose identity the later sync runs under or stops a different user on the same browser from submitting the first driver's queued handovers.","ref":"Q-10"},{"decision":"When a temperature-history gap affects stock, should the stock be automatically placed On Hold while the gap is unresolved, or should the gap be flagged for review without automatically changing stock status? → Flag the gap for review and show the API-returned stock status; do not automatically place the stock On Hold.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"ASM-2 (flag the gap for review without automatically placing stock On Hold) and ASM-18 (keep affected stock On Hold until resolved) directly conflict, and REQ-21 defers to 'the stock status returned by the API' instead of settling which rule applies.","ref":"Q-11"},{"decision":"May a temperature-profile version have an effective date in the past, and if so, how should recalculated results affect stock that was already released or had a quality decision? → Require effective dates to be today or later; do not recalculate earlier decisions.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"AC-6.2 and AC-6.4 allow backdated profile versions that recalculate earlier decisions, but Q-8 never approved backdating, and nothing says what happens to stock already released or already approved by quality that now fails the recalculated budget.","ref":"Q-12"}],"spec":{"assumptions":["If a driver records actions offline and their account is disabled or removed before synchronization, should those queued actions be accepted into the shared record? → assumed: No; online only.","Staff sign in through Meridian Microsoft accounts; customers use email/password, an emailed one-time code, and an emailed reset link, as specified in US-001; ASM-23's no-social/no-SSO constraint applies to customer sign-in, while the one-time code remains required.","The web app presents access, persistence, revocation, and workflow outcomes returned by the separate API; API authorization and data isolation are not asserted by UI requirements.","For temperature-history gaps, the gap is flagged for quality review without automatically placing affected stock On Hold; the web app shows the review status and API-returned stock status and shows no charge to an unobserved temperature tier.","Warehouse-local time governs cutoff, working-day, holiday, delivery-date, and route rules; dates and times are displayed in the user's local zone with the warehouse zone identified.","Numeric policy values stated in the drafts include a 15-minute silence interval, two-minute alert target, 25% budget warning, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction; server calculations and timing are API-side.","Logger gateway and inbound exports use the supplier's documented interface and file format; gateway ingestion is API-side. The logger export is separate from receipt-evidence files; separate evidence uploads, if used, are images or PDFs up to 10 MB each and are kept in cloud storage. The supported format contract needs confirmation.","Supported browsers are the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox; WCAG 2.1 AA applies to main flows.","The source request ends during US-009; driver behavior is limited to stated intent spans and Q-3/Q-4 decisions, with no unstated behavior inferred.","Recall responses record quantity and disposition per affected delivery, reconciling located, used, returned, disposed of, or otherwise accounted-for quantities; supporting documents are not required.","Planning volumes are up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year plus 5,000 reporting devices.","One minimum shelf-life value is set per customer organisation; customers and Dispatchers cannot set it per order.","When readings are missing, do not charge an assumed temperature tier automatically; the web app shows the gap, review status, and stock status returned by the API.","Treat on-hand as a total and show non-overlapping quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired stock.","Keep the stated numeric policy values fixed: 15-minute silence, two-minute alert target, 25% remaining-budget alert, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction.","A System Administrator sets one minimum remaining shelf-life value per customer organisation; Dispatchers and customers cannot change it per order.","Use the serving warehouse's configured local time zone for its cut-off, working-day, and route rules; display dates and times in the user's local zone with the warehouse zone identified.","No existing spreadsheet or operational data is migrated; the system starts empty with seed data for setup.","Use the supplier gateway's existing documented batch API; Meridian provides interface documentation, credentials, and sample payloads.","Alerts are sent by email from fixed templates; no SMS or push notifications.","Who created and last changed each record, and when, are retained; no full audit trail is required.","Provide on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is required.","The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox are supported.","WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.","For each affected delivery, record the customer's response, quantity, and stated disposition; accept the response as accounted for without supporting documents.","Support up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year in addition to 5,000 reporting devices.","If a driver records actions offline and their account is disabled before those actions synchronize, queued actions are not accepted into the shared record.","When a logger or sensor has a reading gap, do not charge an assumed temperature tier automatically; flag the gap for quality review and show the stock status returned by the API.","A customer recall response reconciles each quantity as located, used, returned, disposed of, or otherwise accounted for.","No existing paper-record or spreadsheet information is migrated; the system starts empty with seed data for setup.","Use Meridian's existing supplier gateway and documented interface, and accept the supplier's documented inbound logger export format.","Excursion and route alerts use email only from fixed templates; no SMS or push.","Customer users use email and password, an emailed one-time code, and an emailed reset link; customer social sign-in and customer SSO are excluded. Staff use Meridian Microsoft accounts.","Who created and last changed each record, and when, are retained; no full audit trail is required.","The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox are supported.","WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.","Use the configured local time zone of the serving warehouse for order cut-offs, working days, delivery dates, and route times.","Support up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year in addition to 5,000 reporting devices."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths 320, 768, and 1280/1440 CSS pixels, zero horizontal overflow; phone interactive targets are at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels.","text":"Every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of the agreed main-flow screens pass WCAG 2.1 AA checks; zero unmet applicable success criteria in audited main flows.","text":"Main staff, customer, and driver web flows conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"100% of agreed main-flow UI test cases pass on the latest two versions of each of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","text":"The responsive portals support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"1,000 users, 100,000 records in the first year, and data from 5,000 devices reporting at once.","text":"The web portal supports the stated first-year user and record volume and displays data from the stated simultaneous device volume."}],"outOfScope":["API-side durable persistence, server-side role and organisation enforcement, session revocation, server-side validation and workflow transitions, stock and allocation concurrency/invariants, policy calculations, expiry processing, recall blocking, and database-level audit retention; web requirements cover presentation of API responses.","API-side supplier-gateway ingestion, reading deduplication and reordering, sensor-scale ingestion and processing, silence and excursion detection, stability-budget recalculation, hold placement, and alert timing; web requirements cover returned histories, statuses, and alerts.","API-side email alert and password-reset or one-time-code delivery. SMS and native push channels are excluded; where notification is needed in the web product, it is represented by in-app notice or email as specified by the source requirements.","Historical spreadsheet or paper-record import is excluded; setup uses seed data.","A full immutable audit trail beyond returned creator and last-change identity and timestamps is excluded.","A custom report builder is excluded.","Native iOS/Android binaries and app-store publication are excluded; requested driver functions are delivered in the responsive web app."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in staff or customer user has portal access","id":"AC-1.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows links to the modules permitted for that user, including applicable stock, order, delivery, temperature, quality, and recall pages","when":"the user opens portal navigation"},{"given":"A user opens an available workflow at phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths","id":"AC-1.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen content has no horizontal overflow and phone controls have touch targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels","when":"the page is rendered"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide role-oriented portal pages and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls on phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3","I-4","I-15","ASM-13"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A staff user opens staff sign-in","id":"AC-2.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the Meridian Microsoft sign-in option and no external staff-account form","when":"the user selects the staff sign-in flow"},{"given":"The API returns a one-time-code challenge after a customer submits email and password","id":"AC-2.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a code-entry field, no customer social sign-in or single-sign-on option, and no customer account content before a successful code response","when":"the customer submits the credentials"},{"given":"A customer user requests a password reset","id":"AC-2.3","level":"ui","then":"the request contains the customer email address and the screen shows the reset-link-by-email confirmation returned by the API","when":"the reset request is submitted"},{"given":"A disabled or removed account attempts online sign-in or access","id":"AC-2.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows an access-denied message and no protected page or record is displayed","when":"the API returns an access-denied response"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide staff authentication through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer authentication using email and password followed by a one-time code, with reset links requested by email and no social sign-in or single-sign-on option for customer accounts.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-7","ASM-23"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API returns records for a staff member's assigned warehouses or a customer's organisation","id":"AC-3.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows only the returned records","when":"the user opens the corresponding list"},{"given":"A Quality Manager or Auditor opens a warehouse-scoped list and the API returns all-warehouse records","id":"AC-3.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned records from all warehouses","when":"the list is displayed"},{"given":"An Auditor opens a record page","id":"AC-3.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows record details without create, edit, or delete controls, and an API-refused write is shown as an error message","when":"the page renders"},{"given":"A protected request is refused because the account or record is inaccessible","id":"AC-3.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows an access-ended or access-denied message and clears protected record fields","when":"the web app receives the refusal"}],"ears":"When a user opens portal views, the Meridian responsive web app shall show records and actions returned for that user's role, assigned warehouses, and customer organisation, present Auditor views as read-only, and clear protected data when the API refuses access.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-7","ASM-1","ASM-17","ASM-11","ASM-23"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Customer Administrator opens user management for their organisation","id":"AC-4.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the invitation or removal status returned by the API","when":"the administrator submits an invitation or removal"},{"given":"The API refuses a user-management action, including an action for another organisation","id":"AC-4.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned error message and does not show the other organisation's user as changed","when":"the administrator submits the action"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall let a Customer Administrator invite and remove users through controls scoped to that administrator's customer organisation.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-7"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A System Administrator searches by product name or code or opens a deactivated product","id":"AC-5.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows matching product records and identifies deactivated products as unavailable for ordering","when":"the API returns matching products and active states"},{"given":"A System Administrator submits an incomplete profile or one with overlapping or gapped tiers","id":"AC-5.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the validation error returned by the API and does not show the product as saved","when":"the administrator attempts to save"},{"given":"A System Administrator submits a valid profile with tiers, reason, and effective date","id":"AC-5.3","level":"ui","then":"the request includes the profile tiers, reason, and effective date and the screen shows the new profile version returned by the API","when":"the profile change is submitted"},{"given":"A product has multiple profile versions","id":"AC-5.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists earlier versions with their returned values, reason, effective date, and creator where returned, and provides no edit controls for earlier versions","when":"a user opens profile history"},{"given":"A System Administrator deactivates a product","id":"AC-5.5","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the product as deactivated","when":"the API returns the updated product status"},{"given":"A System Administrator enters a profile effective date before today","id":"AC-5.6","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a validation error and no profile-save request is sent","when":"the administrator attempts to save the profile"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall let System Administrators list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowance or not-permitted designations, a reason, and an effective date no earlier than today, while keeping earlier versions read-only.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","I-10","ASM-4","Q-12"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API returns a new effective profile version and recalculated values for stock still held from the effective date onward","id":"AC-6.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the new version's effective date and the returned budget and decision values","when":"a user opens the profile and affected stock views"},{"given":"A profile version has an effective date of today or later and the API returns an earlier quality decision for affected stock","id":"AC-6.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the earlier decision's returned values and status unchanged and does not show a recalculated earlier decision","when":"a user opens the profile and affected stock views"},{"given":"A System Administrator submits a profile change with a reason and effective date","id":"AC-6.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the new version, reason, effective date, and returned recalculated budget and decision values","when":"the API returns the updated profile and affected-stock results"},{"given":"A profile version takes ef