, and route views.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-11","I-12","I-15","I-17","ASM-5","Q-6","Q-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Warehouse Operator opens the packing form","id":"AC-17.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen provides fields for box type, logger identifier, delivery stop, products, lots, and quantities","when":"the form renders"},{"given":"The operator selects stock, a box type, and logger and submits the packing action","id":"AC-17.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned compatibility result or error message and does not show an unsuccessful box as sealed","when":"the API returns compatibility results or refuses an incompatible band, box type, missing logger, or already-associated logger"},{"given":"A box is ready to be sealed and sealing succeeds","id":"AC-17.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows exactly one logger requirement and the returned seal time, operator, contents, quantities, and logger","when":"the operator opens the box record"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show compatibility, contents, and sealing details returned by the API.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-12","I-13"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Dispatcher creates a route","id":"AC-18.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen provides fields for one vehicle, one driver, route date, at least one ordered stop, and planned arrival times","when":"the route form is displayed"},{"given":"The API refuses confirmation because a box exceeds its qualified duration after applying the configured safety margin, which defaults to 4 hours","id":"AC-18.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the refused status, affected box, returned overage amount, and returned configured safety-margin value","when":"the Dispatcher views the result"},{"given":"A confirmed route is changed before the driver has left for an affected stop"