 order","id":"AC-24.6","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned result for that action and does not mark a refused handover as completed or accepted","when":"the action synchronizes and the API returns an acceptance or refusal"},{"given":"The browser has cached route or delivery data, including recipient details","id":"AC-24.7","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the sign-in or access-denied page and no cached route, stop, delivery, or recipient details","when":"the driver signs out, the cached workday ends, or an API response reports refused access or a disabled account, and the driver next opens the driver experience"},{"given":"One or more actions remain queued after the originating driver signs out or the cached workday ends, and a different user signs in on the same browser","id":"AC-24.8","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows no originating driver's route, recipient details, or queued-action details, and the browser sends no synchronization request for the originating driver's actions","when":"that different user opens the driver experience or reconnects"},{"given":"One or more actions remain queued after the originating driver signs out or the cached workday ends","id":"AC-24.9","level":"ui","then":"the synchronization request uses that driver's authenticated identity and the screen shows the returned result for each queued action","when":"that same driver signs in again with an enabled account and reconnects"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide an installable, responsive driver experience that caches the current workday's assigned route, queues supported loading and delivery actions for synchronization when connectivity returns, retains unsynchronized actions tied to the originating driver across sign-out and workday end, synchronizes those actions only after that same driver signs in again, clears cached route and delivery data when the driver signs out, the workday ends, or access is refused, erases or marks queued actions r