n affected delivery recall response form","id":"AC-26.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen provides fields for response, quantity, and stated disposition for each delivery and returned quantity categories for locating, using, returning, disposing of, or otherwise accounting for units","when":"the form is displayed"},{"given":"A customer submits a recall quantity reconciliation","id":"AC-26.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows submitted quantities, stated dispositions, and returned accounted-for status without requiring supporting-document upload","when":"the API returns the response status"},{"given":"A recall has unreconciled quantities","id":"AC-26.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the outstanding quantity count and affected customer responses returned by the API","when":"a Quality Manager opens its progress page"},{"given":"A Quality Manager starts a recall for one or more lots","id":"AC-26.5","level":"ui","then":"the request includes the selected lots and reason, and the screen shows the recall record and status returned by the API","when":"the Quality Manager selects the lots, enters a reason, and submits the recall"},{"given":"A Quality Manager closes a recall","id":"AC-26.6","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the recall status returned by the API","when":"the Quality Manager submits the close action"},{"given":"The API refuses a recall start or close action","id":"AC-26.7","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned error message and does not show the recall as successfully started or closed","when":"the Quality Manager submits that action"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Quality Managers start recalls by selecting affected lots and providing a reason, view and manage recall records, and close recalls, and let customer users submit a quantity and stated disposition for each affected delivery, showing returned reconciliation and stock-block information.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-17","ASM-15","ASM-19"